.gradle/
build/
# Gradle's output directories are `build/`, and so is one of the three folders
# under tools/, which is a real one holding the release script. The rule above
# matches a directory of that name at any depth, so it swallowed tools/build
# whole: `dist.py` is named by both the README and CLAUDE.md as how a release
# is cut and has never been committed, because `git status` never mentioned it.
# The directory has to be re-included rather than its contents: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a rule naming a file inside one is
# never even read.
!tools/build/
local.properties
.kotlin/
.idea/
*.iml
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
tools/mapdata/liberty_source.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Xcode's per user state: which files were open, which scheme was last run.
# The project and the shared scheme are committed, this is not.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserdatad/
.DS_Store

# Signing keys, never commit
*.jks
*.keystore
# Except the development key, which is committed so every machine signs the
# same way and an APK from one installs over an APK from another. It is not a
# store key: its password is in androidApp/build.gradle.kts.
!androidApp/key0.jks

# The device save tools/build/push_save.sh copies out before it pushes. It is a
# player's own save, it is next to the caller because sqlite3 here is a Windows
# binary that cannot read /tmp, and two of them were committed once by accident.
mapexplore-device-*.db
.mapexplore-push.tmp.db

# The server's own environment: the compose file reads it and it holds a password.
# .env.example is committed and is the one to copy.
.env

# Local APK outputs
androidApp/release/
androidApp/debug/
dist/

# Screenshots pulled off a device while measuring. They are evidence for one
# afternoon, not for the repository.
emu.png
crop.png
*-check.png

# atrace captures pulled by tools/bench/bench_trace.sh, hundreds of megabytes each
trace.txt
# The raw Overpass answer, cached so the POI pipeline can be re-measured without
# asking a public API the same very large question again. Regenerable, 17 MB, and
# nine polite requests to somebody else's server
tools/mapdata/data/overpass_raw.json

# Scratch space for provider research: captured API responses and device screenshots.
.research/
